    <string name="dsh_backup_rescue_desc">Everything above goes through the dsh-config-manager plugin, which lives inside DSH — if DSH will not start, neither will it. The same project also ships a standalone CLI that does not depend on the DSH runtime at all, so it is the first thing to reach for when configuration is broken or you are restoring onto a new machine. Installing or updating the plugin does not give you the CLI command: it must be installed separately with the first command below.</string>
